spoint TREE rendering SPEED optimized at FULL RESOLUTION (user directive: do NOT mask with DPR downscale - it hides real cost). Commit dcccc8de. Full-res fps 23.9 -> 52.1 (2.2x) on AMD Radeon iGPU, 2662 trees + 298 rocks, tris 124k, 0 errors. THREE real fixes (not resolution):
1. app.js adaptive DPR controller DEFAULT OFF (opt-in window.__dprAuto) - resolution downscale masks geometry cost.
2. Vegetation.js capGeo(): LOD0 branch capped 2200 tris / leaf 1400 (raw ez-tree branches ~10k tris); every LOD derives from capped base. cfg.branchTriCap/leafTriCap override.
3. Vegetation.js SHADOW CASTING capped to 35m (branch.addShadowLOD(b2,0) then addShadowLOD(makeEmptyGeo(),SHADOW_CAST=35); cfg.shadowCastDistance). THIS WAS THE BIGGEST WIN (24->52fps): frame decomposition proved DISTANT-TREE SHADOW CASTING was ~20ms (a full geometry pass into the 1024 shadow map for imperceptible far shadows). Near shadows preserved.

BOTTLENECK CHAIN (all witnessed via in-browser frame decomposition - toggle window.__veg._meshes[].branch/leaf.visible, window.__rocks._meshes[].im.visible, sun.castShadow; measure rAF fps): originally geometry-bound (branches) + shadow-bound. After fixes: veg COLOR pass now ~2ms (cheap), veg SHADOW capped, rocks ~2ms. THE REMAINING CEILING is the tv8 PLANET BACKDROP (client/core/TerrainBackdrop.js renderPlanet / mapspinner GPU): ~48-50fps base WITH ZERO veg -> trees are now well-optimized, further big gains require optimizing the planet render (vp-planet-backdrop-floor / vp-tv8-terrain-perf), a separate subsystem. CAVEAT: only measure steady fps after window.__vegProfile.impostors===5 + totalInstances stable (impostor/rock bakes stall multi-second).